  "notes": "Measured on B-58551's right side (2026-03-16), flipped nose-left and fitted to the A350-1000 shape; checked against its left side the same day. Layout assumed the same on both sides (the left photo agrees on titles, sweep and fin). The weave is too fine for areas: the fin and sweep are navy, the weave is the SJX/weave entry. B-58553 flies in an all-grey special (not this scheme). Winglets not seen clearly; left out. Small registration and 'A350-1000' lettering not drawn.",
  "history": "New file (STARLUX had no scheme here). Its only standard scheme since the airline's first flights in 2020."
